laps 6-8 2S discriminator (grid rested >5 min before lap6): lap6 -100 cold: DMM 6.15-6.13, chip B-A 6.15, I 1.71 A. lap7 +100 warm: DMM missed, chip A-B 6.22, I 1.70. lap8 -100 warm: DMM 6.16-6.11, chip 6.13, I 1.70. Grid hot to the touch after.
FINDING: heating is NOT the cause (cold = warm reverse within 0.2%). Direction effect is real: reverse terminal voltage 2.4% below forward on a passive load, seen by chip dividers and DMM alike, while the shunt chain reads the same current both ways (+/-0.5%). => board-D current chain has a ~2% direction-dependent error; Kelvin/island geometry (entry from B-side vs A-side low FET) is the fitting mechanism, ~1.2 mohm of copper difference suffices. High-side drop asymmetric too: 0.13 V fwd vs 0.25 V rev at 1.7 A. Chain scale vs grid route: +2% fwd, +3% rev, bracket ~3%.
